 the saved index stays: the cursor lands on root row 1 ('learn'). The baseline put it on row 0. Reproducer pocs/pr13012-back-from-search.js (green tripwire), re-run by this reviewer: exit 0 on the evaluated tree (landed_row 'learn'), exit 1 on the 67b0e44f product files (landed_index 0). Consequence is cursor placement only; Enter on that row would open/run it. Recorded as KI-MENU-BACK-FILTERED-INDEX (open, low, ship_with_known_issue). Suggested fix: save the index only when filterText is empty, or remember the entered row's root-level ancestor id.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":789},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":798},{"id":"pocs/pr13012-back-from-search.js","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-261001-B4CK","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: after a drill-in from a filtered search, does Back put the cursor on an unrelated parent row? (KI-MENU-BACK-FILTERED-INDEX)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Regression test: Back after a filtered drill-in starts on row 0 or on the entered row's root ancestor\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:setActiveMenu","shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:nextSelectable","SW-REQ-261001-B4CK"],"scenario":"drill into a submenu from parent row k, make the parent list shorter than k+1 rows (remembered row hidden by a guard result) before Backspace: does the cursor land on row k mod count rather than the last row?"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"When the remembered row is gone, setActiveMenu sets selectedIndex = restoreSelection.index without clamping. rebuildDisplay -> settleCursor -> nextSelectable(index, 1) reduces it modulo the row count (Menu.qml:583), so an index past the end wraps to an early row, not the last row. Example: the cursor was on row 6 and guard results hide rows while the submenu is open. B4CK says only 'starts from the saved index and settles off disabled rows', and no witness covers an index >= count. Bounded consequence (cursor placement only), but the wrap is untested.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":798},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":583},{"id":"SW-REQ-261001-B4CK","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: if the parent list shrank while the submenu was open, where does the saved-index fallback land?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Witness: Back with the remembered row gone and a shorter parent list\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:goBack","SW-REQ-261001-B4CK","SW-REQ-260922-DE93"],"scenario":"menu-compositor-test.sh live session: cursor on 'nav' (not row 0), Return, then BackSpace (and a second run with Left): is .rows[.selectedIndex].itemId == \"nav\" after Back?"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The PR author's own 'Before marking ready' item says the graphical session was unavailable, so the keyboard paths were never tried live. The fork's live test test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh:358-361 drills into 'nav' and presses BackSpace, but it asserts only activeMenu and navStack length, not the restored cursor row. That assertion had to change from .navStack[0] == \"root\" to .navStack[0].menu == \"root\" because the PR changes the record shape (dogfood proof work; that test is not in upstream). No live run is recorded in this package.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh","kind":"file","line":359},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1237},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title